  "claim_boundary": "Numerical oracle on real expert weights and real activations. The bound is SOUND: rows it certifies are provably zero after ReLU^2, so skipping them leaves the output bit-identical, and rows it does not certify are still computed exactly. This is NOT a low-rank surrogate and never replaces a weight. The residual row norms are treated as free here; a built version would have to store them (one float per row per expert) and pay the rank-r projection, which the projection_pays_off field accounts for but does not time. No kernel was written and nothing here is a time or throughput measurement."
